<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Dialogs.MessageBoxWindow"
        Title="TanMenu"
        SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        MinWidth="300"
        Background="{DynamicResource SurfaceBaseBrush}">

  <!--
    Deliberately styled by the app-wide DEFAULT control set, not by Themes/Fluent2/Launcher.axaml,
    which is the launcher's identity. An alert is a platform surface and should look like one; the
    launcher's acrylic flyout chrome around a two-line question would read as decoration. Nothing
    here carries a tm- class, so Launcher.axaml cannot reach it, and it still picks up the UI font
    from Tokens.axaml like every other standard control.

    WHICH theme "the default set" means changed under this file in Round 7, Task 3; the rule above
    did not. Themes/Aero/AeroResources.axaml now publishes a ControlTheme keyed {x:Type Button}, and
    the buttons the code-behind builds set no Theme, so they resolve to it instead of to FluentTheme's
    — Application.Styles is searched last-first and Aero is listed after FluentTheme. Measured on the
    恢复 confirm box at 150 % scale, before = a build of eb46249 driven to the same dialog:

        each button   84 x 33.3 DIP Fluent pill  →  84 x 22 DIP Aero double border + gradient
                      (the code-behind's MinWidth=84 governs the width in both; only height moved)
        this window   170.7 DIP tall             →  159.3 DIP tall
        corner radius Tokens' ControlCornerRadius 4 → Aero's own 3 (outer) / 2 (inner)

    That is the wanted answer rather than a leak: a Windows 7 message box drew exactly this button,
    so no Theme= is pinned here to hold the Fluent one back. What this file does NOT get is the
    launcher's hand-drawn Aero caption (Round 7 Task 1 replaced MainWindow's alone) — a system caption
    is right for a platform surface.

    Buttons are created in code-behind: their count, order, labels (localized) and default/cancel
    roles all depend on the MessageBoxButtons value.
  -->
  <StackPanel Margin="22,20">
    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="14">
      <Border Name="IconHost"
              Width="30" Height="30"
              CornerRadius="15"
              IsVisible="False"
              VerticalAlignment="Top">
        <TextBlock Name="IconGlyph"
                   Foreground="White"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   FontSize="17"
                   HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                   VerticalAlignment="Center" />
      </Border>
      <TextBlock Name="MessageText"
                 MaxWidth="420"
                 TextWrapping="Wrap"
                 VerticalAlignment="Center" />
    </StackPanel>

    <StackPanel Name="ButtonRow"
                Orientation="Horizontal"
                Spacing="8"
                Margin="0,22,0,0"
                HorizontalAlignment="Right" />
  </StackPanel>

</Window>
